review:
So i finally went to play Splinter Cell Blacklist as i initially was skeptical to buy it at release, then MGSV came out and i was like “i just cant go back to play Splinter Cell with a cover system”. I can safely say that Ubi Toronto took everything that was best from the previous games, without any previous experience with the series, and actually managed to produce the most fluid and best hardcore Splinter Cell experience. This game plays fantastically well, they did everything right with it and they did not even have to compromise the hardcore experience so that casual gamers can enjoy it too.
Here's a list with what the game has to offer:
[list]
    [*]great mission design;
    [*]more than one seed pattern for enemy movement;
    [*]hardcore stealth option to not disturb enemies;
    [*]cover system that is not only snap to cover, but also has fluidity in sprinting over obstacles;
    [*]customizable weapons and gadgets;
    [*]the great coop experience from Conviction is back and just as good as ever;
    [*]missions that can be played either solo or coop, with extra alternative paths that you can use only in coop;
    [*]the mark & execute system from Conviction returns, which is also disabled on the hardest difficulty, but you can still just mark without executing up to 3 enemies (very helpful especially in coop);
    [*]remember Spies vs Mercs? Now you can enjoy that again as well.
[/list]
